# Crystal Imperium play test: the battle health box's name after a switch (BW battle UI). A name
# is printed in the font that fits it into 7 tiles, and on the player's side it runs into the
# health box's second sprite; until 0.10.1 only 6 tiles were cleared first, so after FERALIGATR
# a shorter name kept the tail of its R ("LARVITAR -|", reported on Delta). Here ONIX is sent out,
# switched for FERALIGATR and back: its name strip (y 74-87, below the opponent's Pokemon, which
# the AI may switch), 30 frames into the action menu the first time, must look exactly the same
# within one bob of the health box (37 frames) the second time: the bob doesn't always start in
# the same phase (it didn't on VBA-M after the opponent's hit in 0.13.0), and a leftover R would
# never match.
# Action menu cursor: 0 FIGHT, 1 BAG, 2 POKEMON, 3 RUN; it is back on FIGHT every turn.
!new_game()
!give_mon(95, 21)
!give_mon(160, 21)
!no_care_packages()
!battle_trainer(402)
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 4000 A onix_action_menu
wait 30
shot 01_onix.png
snaprect onix_name 136 74 78 14
# POKEMON > FERALIGATR (second slot) > SHIFT
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 90
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 30
press A
wait 60
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 4000 B feraligatr_action_menu
wait 30
shot 02_feraligatr.png
# And back to ONIX
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 90
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 30
press A
wait 60
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 4000 B onix_again_action_menu
wait 30
shot 03_onix_again.png
!expect_battler(0, "species", "SPECIES_ONIX", "onix_back_in")
expectrectwithin onix_name 40 no_leftover_of_feraligatr
